{"type":"step-attempt","step":"code-review","sessionId":"2a835f07-9545-4d67-bb90-6fb270e02892","outcome":{"verdict":"approved","findingsPath":"specrunner/changes/cli-handler-exit-boundary/review-feedback-001.md","error":null,"toolResult":{"ok":true,"findings":[{"severity":"medium","resolution":"fixable","file":"src/cli/__tests__/command-registry-reopen.test.ts","title":"False-positive tests: TC-004-registry-c and TC-012-b always pass regardless of contract","rationale":"Both tests use `expect.fail('Expected process.exit(2) to be called')` inside a catch that then checks `msg.toMatch(/process\\.exit\\(2\\)/)`. Under the new return-value contract the handler returns 2 without calling process.exit, causing expect.fail to throw an AssertionError whose message *contains* the substring 'process.exit(2)', which satisfies the regex. The tests pass as false positives and will not detect a regression to the old process.exit-calling pattern. TC-004-registry-d covers the behavior correctly with the new contract.","line":107},{"severity":"low","resolution":"fixable","file":"src/cli/__tests__/command-registry-reopen.test.ts","title":"getReopenHandler() return type annotation still says Promise<void>","rationale":"The helper function types the handler return as `Promise<void>` but the new contract is `Promise<number>`. The stale annotation is inconsistent with the refactored contract and could suppress TypeScript errors at call sites, misleading future maintainers.","line":49},{"severity":"low","resolution":"fixable","file":"src/cli/__tests__/exit-contract-harness.ts","title":"configureMocks() async callback not awaited — latent timing race","rationale":"The harness types the parameter as `() => void` and calls it without await. Actual callers pass `async () => { await applySetup(caseDef.setup); }`. Mock setup (await import + mockResolvedValue) races against the specrunner module import. Tests pass because the specrunner import tree is large enough that setup completes first, but the ordering is not guaranteed and could surface as flakiness under different caching conditions.","line":81}],"evidence":{"checked":30,"skipped":0,"unverified":1},"observations":[{"severity":"low","file":"bin/specrunner.ts","title":"stderrWrite / process.stderr.write masking inconsistency is pre-existing","rationale":"Pre-dispatch sections (unknown command, worktree guard, repo guard) use process.stderr.write directly while the dispatch error boundary uses stderrWrite (maskSensitive). Design.md D5 acknowledges this as a pre-existing inconsistency not introduced by R3b."},{"severity":"low","file":"specrunner/changes/cli-handler-exit-boundary/test-cases.md","title":"TC-027 base fixture commit dating requires manual git log verification","rationale":"The base fixture and generator were both added in this branch. Reviewers should confirm via git log that the fixture commit predates production file changes (src/cli/*.ts / bin/specrunner.ts).","line":263}]},"followUpAttempts":1,"transientRetryAttempts":0,"addedTurns":{"reportRetry":0,"postWork":0,"outputRepair":1}},"startedAt":"2026-09-03T15:41:32.554Z","endedAt":"2026-09-03T15:50:22.475Z","commitOid":"b73d6f0283743348f25b027c4f33c16b7beb32d2"}
